# THE INTERRUPT-ENTRY DRAIN CAP, SIZED OVER THE RECORD BOUND PLUS ONE, with the unit case that discriminates it.
# Answers CM209-Low-1, and closes CM208-Info-1, which recorded that no unit case exercised this function.
#
# THE FINDING, every term quoted from the sources this landing changes:
#   gen_tb_pkg.sv:556   return per_record * GEN_IRQ_ENTRY_BOUND_RECORDS + GEN_IRQ_DRAIN_MARGIN_CYCLES;
#     that is the line as it stands at the base commit; the change makes it :558 because the comment above it grows
#     by two lines, and both sides are printed in full in section 1 below
#   gen_env_pkg.sv:377  while ((vif.evt_retired_count - drain_rec0) <= GEN_IRQ_ENTRY_BOUND_RECORDS
# The loop's comparison is AT OR BELOW the bound, so the drain's length is the bound PLUS ONE records, while the cap
# was sized over the bound alone. The extra record was therefore funded only by GEN_IRQ_DRAIN_MARGIN_CYCLES, whose
# own comment gives it a different job, "the finish handshake and the last record's write-back after the drain's
# final retirement". A cap short of the drain's length cannot fail a run; it can only end the drain EARLY, and an
# early end leaves an expectation at age exactly the bound unjudged and reported open with no error, which is the
# silent missed detection the bound-plus-one drain length exists to remove. That is why this is worth fixing even
# though no simulation reaches it.
#
# THE FIGURES, DERIVED FROM THE CONSTANTS. GEN_IRQ_ENTRY_BOUND_RECORDS 17, GEN_IRQ_DRAIN_RECORD_OVERHEAD_CYCLES 2,
# GEN_IRQ_DRAIN_MARGIN_CYCLES 40. At the default effective maxima, which the runs themselves report as i 3/4 and
# d 3/4, per_record is max(3+4, 3+4) + 2 = 9, so the cap moves from 9*17+40 = 193 to 9*18+40 = 202. In general the
# resized cap is the old one plus one per_record, so it still tracks the bus maxima.
#
# WHERE THE OLD SIZING ACTUALLY BREAKS, which is what the unit case exercises. Borrowing the margin works only while
# one record costs less than the margin: the old cap covers the drain's length exactly when per_record is at most
# GEN_IRQ_DRAIN_MARGIN_CYCLES. At the default maxima per_record is 9 against a margin of 40, so the old cap DID
# cover the extra record, which is why no simulation red exists. Push one record above the margin and the borrowing
# fails. A unit case can set the maxima directly; a simulation that widened them that far starves its own run before
# the drain, which landing 32 measured.

== 1. THE TDD PAIR: the unit case's RED on the committed function and its GREEN after the change ==

   THE FUNCTION BEFORE, printed from the base commit:
       // The interrupt-entry drain's cycle cap, COMPUTED from a run's effective bus maxima rather than frozen: the four
       // gen_{i,d}bus_{gnt,rvalid}_max plusargs overwrite the regime windows with only a lower clamp, so a constant taken
       // from the defaults would be wrong for any run that widens one. Worst legitimate per-record cost is the slower
       // bus's grant plus response wait plus the pipeline's own stages, times the entry bound, plus the margin.
       function automatic int unsigned gen_irq_drain_cap_cycles(int unsigned i_gnt_max, int unsigned i_rvalid_max,
                                                                int unsigned d_gnt_max, int unsigned d_rvalid_max);
         int unsigned ibus_cost = i_gnt_max + i_rvalid_max;
         int unsigned dbus_cost = d_gnt_max + d_rvalid_max;
         int unsigned per_record = (ibus_cost > dbus_cost ? ibus_cost : dbus_cost) + GEN_IRQ_DRAIN_RECORD_OVERHEAD_CYCLES;
         return per_record * GEN_IRQ_ENTRY_BOUND_RECORDS + GEN_IRQ_DRAIN_MARGIN_CYCLES;
       endfunction

   THE FUNCTION AFTER, printed from the tree as this landing hands it:
       // The interrupt-entry drain's cycle cap, COMPUTED from a run's effective bus maxima rather than frozen: the four
       // gen_{i,d}bus_{gnt,rvalid}_max plusargs overwrite the regime windows with only a lower clamp, so a constant taken
       // from the defaults would be wrong for any run that widens one. Worst legitimate per-record cost is the slower
       // bus's grant plus response wait plus the pipeline's own stages, times the DRAIN'S LENGTH, which is the
       // entry bound plus one record because the drain runs while the count is at or below the bound. The margin
       // is left to the finish handshake and the last write-back, so the extra record is not borrowed from it.
       function automatic int unsigned gen_irq_drain_cap_cycles(int unsigned i_gnt_max, int unsigned i_rvalid_max,
                                                                int unsigned d_gnt_max, int unsigned d_rvalid_max);
         int unsigned ibus_cost = i_gnt_max + i_rvalid_max;
         int unsigned dbus_cost = d_gnt_max + d_rvalid_max;
         int unsigned per_record = (ibus_cost > dbus_cost ? ibus_cost : dbus_cost) + GEN_IRQ_DRAIN_RECORD_OVERHEAD_CYCLES;
         return per_record * (GEN_IRQ_ENTRY_BOUND_RECORDS + 1) + GEN_IRQ_DRAIN_MARGIN_CYCLES;
       endfunction

   HOW TO RUN IT. The check is a pure-SV unit test and is run BY HAND today: nothing under ci or the flow
   invokes it, so a worktree gate that runs the Python unit tests will not pick it up. Run it from the repo
   root, after sourcing the site environment, with these four commands and read the summary line:
     source ci/env.sh
     vcs -full64 -sverilog -timescale=1ns/10ps -f dv/auto_dv/tb/unit/gen_ut_drain_cap.f \
         -top gen_ut_drain_cap_top -Mdir=<outdir>/csrc -o <outdir>/simv -l <outdir>/compile.log
     <outdir>/simv -l <outdir>/run.log
     command grep -a "GEN_UT_DRAIN_CAP" <outdir>/run.log
   The filelist dv/auto_dv/tb/unit/gen_ut_drain_cap.f names four sources and no RTL beyond ibex_pkg:
     // filelist of the gen_irq_drain_cap_cycles unit test (no RTL, no UVM test); compile with -sverilog
