   READING: both builds retire 18 records in 126 cycles with nothing open and zero irq_entry errors, and only
   the printed cap moves, 193 to 202. The pair shows the change compiles and that the drain completes on the
   eighteenth record inside the new cap; it is NOT a discriminating red and is not offered as one. Section 1
   is the discriminating check.

   IDENTITIES. Neither build's shape is a committed one, so no gate identity (the flow's filelist_digest over
   gen_rtl.f plus gen_tb.f) applies to either and none is claimed. The figures printed are the local runner's
   find-digest over dv/auto_dv env, tb, isa and gen_tb. The base build's figure is the one HEAD's sources
   produce, which is the cross-check that the base really is the base.

== 4. WHAT THIS LANDING DOES NOT CLAIM ==
   It does not claim a simulation ever hit the old cap. At the default maxima truncating an 18-record drain
   would need more than 193/18 = 10.7 cycles per record against a modelled worst case of 9, so it cannot
   happen there, and landing 32 already measured that widening the instruction bus starves the RUN before it
   stretches the DRAIN (rvalid_max 12 and 200 both died before the drain). The unreachability holds for
   records that cost no more than the MODEL allows; a record can exceed it only if something outside the bus
   model holds retirement, which is the retirement-stall residual landing 31 left out and the plan already
   records as owed, not a second hole. The reachable-in-principle regime is per_record above the margin, and
   section 1 is where that regime is exercised.
